From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [vllm] fix: the sub-paged attention view of FlashInfer's
 fused K/V layout under HND

Local, from no pull request. LMCache pull request #4253 (1847435f) re-views the fused layout for NHD only; its own
design document names HND as a limitation, and draft pull request #5390 targets it.

vLLM's FlashInfer backend registers each attention layer as a fused-K/V rank-4 tensor
(pages, num_kv_heads, kernel_block_size, 2 * head_size) and allows only HND layouts on Blackwell. Since #4253
_SubpagedAttentionViewEdit re-views it at the scheduler block size as an NHD-shaped rank-5 tensor, whose block size
the format detector reads under HND from the synthetic heads axis (1): LMCache classifies the attention group as
compressed, and store and retrieve move a fraction of each block's KV, corrupting live KV on every load. Under HND
the rank-4 tensor is now re-viewed in its own memory order as (blocks, 1, block_size, num_kv_heads * content), which
the detector reads at the scheduler block size; with one KV head per rank the dims stay semantic. Each group's kind,
block size, page size, layout and registered tensor shape are logged once at registration.

What the port takes and changes:
- The patch's fused re-view, _apply_fused, for HND only; under NHD v0.5.8rc1's re-view from #4253 stays, which does
  the job of the patch's NHD-strided rank-4 view. vLLM 0.34 resolves LBHNC (the "HND" hint) for FlashInfer on
  Blackwell; with its other choice there, the blocks-first BLHNC, it keeps kernel blocks at the scheduler block size,
  so no sub-paged edit applies.
- The patch's rank-5 change (matching on both candidate token dims, the kernel block size from dim 3 under HND) is
  left out: vLLM registers a rank-5 tensor in NHD order under HND too, with the heads at dim 3, and v0.5.8rc1
  deliberately rejects a rank-5 tensor it cannot re-view correctly, while reading dim 3 would re-view an HND-ordered
  one into the NHD-shaped view the detector misreads. vLLM 0.28 and 0.34 register rank 4 for FlashInfer.
- The patch's docstring change to _SubpagedMLAAttentionViewEdit.apply, which changed no code there, is left out.
- The registration log reads each group's first layer spec (v0.5.8rc1 keeps per-layer specs for a group of uniform
  types) and shows a (K, V) plane tuple like a list.
- docs/design/integration/vllm/kv_cache_group_edits.md says what HND does now; it said HND is not reached by default.
- tests/v1/test_vllm_kv_cache_group_edits.py covers the HND re-view, its detection as NL_X_NB_NH_BS_CS at the
  scheduler block size (detect_format and get_block_size from lmcache.v1.common since #6530), and the refusal of a
  non-contiguous HND tensor; the patch had no test.
